  "version": "as-filed",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(other) Sec 1: rewrites Texas Constitution Art. IV, Sec. 22 and adds (b): \"The Attorney General shall have concurrent jurisdiction with each county or district attorney of this State to represent this State in the prosecution of a criminal offense prescribed by the election laws of this State.\"\n(other) Sec 2: election date November 4, 2025 and ballot proposition wording.\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
